      "locator": "refined markdown lines 1862-1871, 6614-6658, 7376-7468",
      "safe_claims": [
        "A truss uses triangular rigidity and linear members primarily in axial tension or compression.",
        "Top and bottom chords, web members, panels, heels, and panel points define truss anatomy.",
        "Loads should be applied at panel points to avoid secondary stresses; purlins away from panel points create local bending in the top chord.",
        "Steel trusses use welded or bolted members and gusset plates.",
        "Warren, Belgian, Fink, Pratt, and Howe trusses are distinguished by web arrangement and tension/compression behavior.",
        "Wood trusses and trussed rafters require bracing, anchorage, manufacturer/engineer guidance, and attention to panel-point loading."
      ],
      "use_limits": [
        "No residential span table by truss name, site wind design rule, tie placement rule, connection tightening value, or timber allowable stress is captured for this batch."
      ],
      "sort_order": 0,
